# Registration content-fingerprint key (e5 chunk 2, E5-SPEC-41/42). Template for
# .env.registration, which is gitignored.
#
# `make up` GENERATES .env.registration with a random 32-byte key if the file is
# missing — it does not copy this template — so no two deployments share a key
# and nobody has to remember a bootstrap step. This file exists so
# `docker compose config/build` can parse the topology in a checkout that has
# never run `make up` (CI seeds it exactly the way it seeds .env.redis and
# .env.ai-proxy).
#
# WHAT THE KEY IS FOR. intake records a keyed digest of the submitted content
# beside the submission_id, and a retry carrying a recorded identifier is
# answered as a replay only if the content matches; an EDITED retry after a lost
# response gets a 409 instead of a confirmation of a chart it never edited.
#
# The key lives in its OWN env file rather than the shared .env because compose
# hands .env to every container: a key there is a key for
# eligibility/records/scheduling/interop/roi/ai-assistant too. Only
# intake-service loads this file — guarded by tests/test_compose_topology.py.
# The scoping matters more here than for the redis password: the fingerprint's
# inputs (DOB, SSN, member id) are guessable, so this key is the only thing
# standing between a stolen `registration_submissions` column and an offline
# confirmation oracle.
#
# FAIL-CLOSED: shipped empty on purpose. With no usable key, POST /intake
# answers 503 rather than fingerprinting PHI under a value every clone shares.
# Presence is NOT the guard — app.py::_fingerprint_key also refuses known
# placeholder values and anything under 32 characters, because a committed
# template value is as published as a hardcoded default (PR #76 review round 3).
# Never put a real value here; generate one instead, or manually with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# ROTATION COST, accepted (plan D-19): rotating invalidates every recorded
# fingerprint, so a lost-confirmation retry straddling the rotation answers 409
# rather than replaying. The operator re-enters on a fresh mount, the second
# chart is queued as a candidate duplicate for human review, and nothing is
# silent. Deliberately NOT added to docs/debt-log.md's remediation runbook step 1
# — that checklist rotates the secrets that reached git history and enumerates
# them from the committed blob, and this key has never been committed.
REGISTRATION_FINGERPRINT_KEY=
